2","shelf":"Backlog","shelves":["Backlog"],"added":"2026-04-18","pf":[],"r":0,"g":["Shooter"],"fr":[],"dev":["Turtle Rock Studios","Valve"],"pub":["Electronic Arts","Valve"],"rel":"2009-11-17","u":"https://www.grouvee.com/games/107187-left-4-dead-2/","rv":"","rvt":"","rvd":"","log":[],"rp":0,"dlcs":[]},{"id":107313,"t":"Saints Row: The Third","shelf":"Played","shelves":["Played"],"added":"2026-04-18","pf":[],"r":5,"g":["Adventure","Racing","Shooter"],"fr":[],"dev":["Volition"],"pub":["CyberFront","Deep Silver","Square Enix","THQ"],"rel":"2011-11-15","u":"https://www.grouvee.com/games/107313-saints-row-the-third/","rv":"SR3 did not shy away from doing everything and anything in its power to be wacky and derailed but that is what made this so much amazing. \nThe writing, the story, the characters, the mechanics, .... its an experience. It helps it stand out as a game that took confidence in being what it was and nailed it. \nIts not everyday one can have an enjoyable experience of this level.","rvt":"The Game that Evolved","rvd":"2026-04-18","log":[],"rp":1,"dlcs":[]},{"id":107315,"t":"Saints Row 2","shelf":"Played","shelves":["Played"],"added":"2026-04-18","pf":[],"r":5,"g":["Adventure","Racing","Shooter"],"fr":[],"dev":["Volition"],"pub":["THQ"],"rel":"2008-10-14","u":"https://www.grouvee.com/games/107315-saints-row-2/","rv":"","rvt":"","rvd":"2026-04-18","log":[],"rp":1,"dlcs":[]},{"id":107317,"t":"Saints Row","shelf":"Played","shelves":["Played"],"added":"2026-04-18","pf":["Xbox 360"],"r":5,"g":["Adventure","Racing","Shooter"],"fr":[],"dev":["Volition"],"pub":["THQ"],"rel":"2006-08-29","u":"https://www.grouvee.com/games/107317-saints-row/","rv":"This is where the famous Saints Row franchise was born. \nWhile it may be a GTA knockoff, it managed to build its own personality, and for me, that was way better than the whole GTA experience. \nIt connects you, it delivers a personalized experience. It makes you feel like part of something big. Even if the game was a normal gang war game (with enjoyable mechanics, storyline, characters and witty writing) the game stands apart. \nThis was the introduction for me to what would become my favorite gaming franchise of all time.","rvt":"The Start of a Legacy","rvd":"2026-04-18","log":[],"rp":0,"dlcs":[]},{"id":107319,"t":"Saints Row IV","shelf":"Played","shelves":["Played"],"added":"2026-04-18","pf":[],"r":5,"g":["Adventure","Shooter"],"fr":[],"dev":["High Voltage Software","Volition"],"pub":["Deep Silver"],"rel":"2013-08-20","u":"https://www.grouvee.com/games/107319-saints-row-iv/","rv":"While its a shame that they reused the map of SR3, \nit doesn't change the fact that this game is so hella fun and crazy with superpowers, aliens and just all out craziness. An open world superhero experience is not your everyday thing. The DLC Gat out of hell is an even crazier experience. \nWhile the final outcome was not what the original developers had in mind, it was still nevertheless an amazing experience. \nI just wish we got more.","rvt":"Superpowers!!!","rvd":"2026-04-18","log":[],"rp":0,"dlcs":[]},{"id":107639,"t":"Doom","shelf":"Wish List","shelves":["Wish List"],"added":"2026-04-18","pf":[],"r":0,"g":["Shooter"],"fr":["Doom"],"dev":["id Software"],"pub":["Bethesda Softworks"],"rel":"2016-05-12","u":"https://www.grouvee.com/games/107639-doom/","rv":"","rvt":"","rvd":"","log":[],"rp":0,"dlcs":[]},{"id":108162,"t":"Uncharted: Drake's Fortune","shelf":"Wish List","shelves":["Wish List"],"added":"2026-04-18","pf":["PlayStation 3"],"r":0,"g":["Adventure","Platform","Shooter"],"fr":["Uncharted"],"dev":["Naughty Dog"],"pub":["Sony Computer Entertainment"],"rel":"2007-11-16","u":"https://www.grouvee.com/games/108162-uncharted-drakes-fortune/","rv":"","rvt":"","rvd":"","log":[],"rp":0,"dlcs":[]},{"id":108496,"t":"Far Cry 3","shelf":"Retired","shelves":["Retired"],"added":"2026-04-18","pf":[],"r":3,"g":["Adventure","Shooter"],"fr":["Far Cry"],"dev":["Ubisoft Montreal"],"pub":["Ubisoft Entertainment"],